WEBVTT

00:00:02.150 --> 00:00:05.980
A young man traveled across the ocean to study music.

00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:11.570
In a far off country, he met a very small and extraordinary creature.

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:17.560
The tiny creature was injured, so feeling pity for it, he treated it.

00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:18.910
Upon doing so...

00:00:20.530 --> 00:00:23.340
I owe you my life.

00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:28.150
For this, I will grant the blessing of music to the school you build.

00:00:30.080 --> 00:00:32.240
Now, some time has passed.

00:00:32.240 --> 00:00:35.090
Another extraordinary encounter has taken place.

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:13.090
The Aloof Virtuoso

00:02:13.090 --> 00:02:16.030
Seiso Academy School-wide Competition

00:02:19.850 --> 00:02:22.970
Sorry to come on such short notice, Len.

00:02:22.970 --> 00:02:26.060
But it's been ages since we've seen you up on stage.

00:02:26.060 --> 00:02:27.290
We're looking forward to it.

00:02:27.730 --> 00:02:31.300
I will try my best to not disappoint your expectations.

00:02:35.620 --> 00:02:40.890
Tsukimori-kun talks that politely to his own parents?

00:02:40.890 --> 00:02:43.150
The evidence is damning.

00:02:43.860 --> 00:02:48.970
His mother is Misa Hamai-san, right?

00:02:48.970 --> 00:02:50.960
She's striking.

00:02:50.960 --> 00:02:52.650
Yes, she really is.

00:02:53.810 --> 00:02:55.600
It's really her.

00:02:56.340 --> 00:02:59.680
Oh, might you be Tsuchiura-kun?

00:02:59.680 --> 00:03:04.000
As a fellow pianist, I am really looking forward to your performance.

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:06.340
I-I'm honored.

00:03:11.980 --> 00:03:13.810
And you're Hino-san, right?

00:03:13.810 --> 00:03:15.000
Y-Yes!

00:03:15.270 --> 00:03:19.630
You're also a General Studies student, right? Good luck.

00:03:19.630 --> 00:03:22.770
Y-Yes. Thank you very much.

00:03:23.770 --> 00:03:25.840
Look, it's Misa Hamai!

00:03:25.840 --> 00:03:28.310
Wow, she's even more beautiful in person.

00:03:28.310 --> 00:03:31.520
I wonder if Tsukimori-kun takes after his mother.

00:03:31.520 --> 00:03:34.110
His father is handsome, but she's...

00:03:34.110 --> 00:03:37.260
Wow, she's really an incredible person.

00:03:44.210 --> 00:03:48.110
I never expected you to be a fan of Tsukimori-kun's mother!

00:03:48.110 --> 00:03:49.240
Shut up!

00:03:49.460 --> 00:03:51.740
Could it be you're getting nervous?

00:03:51.740 --> 00:03:54.670
Of course I am. Anyone would.

00:03:54.670 --> 00:04:02.070
The Second Selection of the Seiso Academy School-wide Music Competition will now begin.

00:04:04.550 --> 00:04:09.950
Performer 1, from General Studies, class 2-5, Ryotaro Tsuchiura-kun.

00:04:10.710 --> 00:04:14.090
Hey, hey, why are you getting so stiff?

00:04:14.090 --> 00:04:15.300
Sheesh.

00:04:15.300 --> 00:04:18.780
Stay calm until I finish my performance.

00:04:19.440 --> 00:04:22.740
Geez, he never gets nervous!

00:04:22.990 --> 00:04:26.750
Performing a Chopin composition, "Fantasie-Impromptu."

00:04:29.920 --> 00:04:32.930
So the new participant, Tsuchiura, is leading off.

00:04:32.930 --> 00:04:33.960
Amo-san...

00:04:33.960 --> 00:04:35.820
It's starting!

00:04:35.820 --> 00:04:38.420
Of course I'm going to be keeping a close eye on Tsukimori-kun,

00:04:38.420 --> 00:04:40.620
but Tsuchiura-kun is not to be missed, either.

00:04:40.620 --> 00:04:44.630
He had that flashy entrance and great performance last time,

00:04:44.630 --> 00:04:47.890
so I think everyone is curious about what he can really do.

00:04:47.890 --> 00:04:49.450
Wow...

00:05:15.810 --> 00:05:18.110
No doubt about it, he's good.

00:05:18.110 --> 00:05:21.840
He's way better than the last time I heard him play!

00:06:05.420 --> 00:06:07.380
He's really talented!

00:06:07.380 --> 00:06:11.220
His touch is so soft... He's really on the soccer team?

00:06:13.460 --> 00:06:17.780
That's pretty wild for a General Studies student to play so well.

00:06:20.920 --> 00:06:22.190
Just kidding.

00:06:22.190 --> 00:06:23.590
Mori-san!

00:06:23.530 --> 00:06:26.460
What's wrong? Are you nervous, Hino-san?

00:06:26.460 --> 00:06:30.020
Of course I am! I have to follow that act!

00:06:30.810 --> 00:06:37.310
Next, performer 2, from General Studies, class 2-2, Kahoko Hino-san.

00:06:37.310 --> 00:06:38.880
I'm up.

00:06:39.640 --> 00:06:41.850
I really am nervous!

00:06:41.850 --> 00:06:44.590
Performing a Pachelbel composition, "Canon."

00:06:44.590 --> 00:06:46.220
Geez...

00:06:46.220 --> 00:06:47.430
Good luck.

00:06:47.430 --> 00:06:48.530
Thanks.

00:06:50.430 --> 00:06:53.460
That's right. I decided to do my best.

00:06:58.050 --> 00:07:03.480
Something to believe in... Mio and Nao taught me how important that is.

00:07:03.480 --> 00:07:09.990
I've stopped worrying about the magic violin or the fact I'm an amateur.

00:07:10.700 --> 00:07:15.590
I don't know if I'm real or a fraud,

00:07:16.670 --> 00:07:20.620
but, today, for what I believe in,

00:07:20.620 --> 00:07:21.940
I'll play.

00:07:48.860 --> 00:07:50.990
She seems at ease out there.

00:07:50.990 --> 00:07:53.360
Yeah, better than in the first selection.

00:08:37.700 --> 00:08:41.150
That was great, Kaho-chan! You were awesome!

00:08:41.150 --> 00:08:42.830
Yeah! You were really great!

00:08:52.550 --> 00:08:55.460
The two General Studies students are really good.

00:08:55.460 --> 00:08:59.010
Especially Tsuchiura... What's he doing in General Studies?

00:08:59.010 --> 00:09:01.470
But Hino has gotten quite good, too.

00:09:01.470 --> 00:09:05.260
Hino-chan! Good job! You were great out there!

00:09:05.260 --> 00:09:07.320
Don't flatter me!

00:09:08.020 --> 00:09:12.780
Ah, it's over. But yet, I still feel so nervous.

00:09:12.780 --> 00:09:18.750
Performer 3, from the Music Department, class 3-B, Kazuki Hihara-kun.

00:09:19.190 --> 00:09:23.250
Performing a Mendelssohn composition, "Auf Flugeln des Gesanges."

00:09:24.280 --> 00:09:26.690
Kanayan, don't forget your promise.

00:09:26.690 --> 00:09:30.120
I know, I know. Now hurry and get on stage.

00:09:30.120 --> 00:09:31.210
Promise?

00:09:31.210 --> 00:09:32.710
Oh, it's nothing.

00:09:47.120 --> 00:09:50.420
Looks like Hihara-sempai's performance has started.

00:09:50.420 --> 00:09:54.250
I shouldn't have to head back until Fuyuumi-san plays after him.

00:10:24.260 --> 00:10:27.450
I should just play like I always do, huh?

00:10:56.860 --> 00:10:58.810
How was I, Kanayan?

00:10:58.810 --> 00:11:00.230
Y-Yeah...

00:11:00.230 --> 00:11:03.150
You were great, Hihara-sempai!

00:11:03.150 --> 00:11:05.020
Thank you, Hino-chan.

00:11:05.810 --> 00:11:09.070
This is bad...

00:11:09.070 --> 00:11:11.490
Huh? Why is it bad?

00:11:11.490 --> 00:11:16.190
If he places in the top three, I have to treat him to whatever he wants to eat.

00:11:16.190 --> 00:11:18.320
Why are you giving him incentives?

00:11:18.810 --> 00:11:21.080
You dug your own grave, though.

00:11:21.080 --> 00:11:27.310
Performer 4, from the Music Department, class 1-B, Shoko Fuyuumi-san.

00:11:27.310 --> 00:11:30.150
Performing a Saint-Saens competition, "Romance."

00:11:30.150 --> 00:11:31.700
OK, Fuyuumi!

00:11:31.700 --> 00:11:34.000
Knock Hihara out of the running!

00:11:34.000 --> 00:11:35.370
U-Umm...

00:11:35.370 --> 00:11:38.390
Sensei! Why are you pressuring her like that?!

00:11:38.390 --> 00:11:39.660
I'm just kidding.

00:11:39.660 --> 00:11:41.440
Sheesh.

00:11:44.510 --> 00:11:47.040
By the way, Sensei, where is Tsukimori?

00:11:47.040 --> 00:11:48.530
Tsukimori?

00:11:48.530 --> 00:11:51.810
I saw him head out a little while ago.

00:11:51.810 --> 00:11:53.630
Maybe he's in the dressing room?

00:11:53.630 --> 00:11:55.220
Waiting room?

00:11:55.220 --> 00:11:57.480
Umm, I'm going to go check on him.

00:11:57.480 --> 00:11:59.280
School-wide Competition - Dressing Room for Participants

00:12:00.270 --> 00:12:02.250
Excuse me!

00:12:03.960 --> 00:12:06.090
Huh? He's not here?

00:12:10.560 --> 00:12:12.040
What's this all about?

00:12:12.040 --> 00:12:16.380
Are you all right, Fuyuumi? You don't look so good.

00:12:16.380 --> 00:12:21.650
Geez, it's cause you had to go and say that right before her performance!

00:12:21.650 --> 00:12:25.800
Oh, sorry about that. But you played well.

00:12:25.800 --> 00:12:29.220
Kanayan, Tsukimori isn't back yet?

00:12:29.220 --> 00:12:33.440
Yeah, I figured, of all people, he'd be OK, but...

00:12:33.440 --> 00:12:35.700
All right. I'll go look for him, too.

00:12:35.700 --> 00:12:37.920
I'll help you, Tsuchiura.

00:12:37.920 --> 00:12:39.600
Sorry. Please do.

00:12:39.600 --> 00:12:45.510
Performer 5, from the Music Department, class 1-A, Keiichi Shimizu-kun.

00:12:45.510 --> 00:12:48.420
Performing a Saint-Saens competition, "Le Cygne."

00:12:48.420 --> 00:12:50.100
And, there you have it.

00:12:50.100 --> 00:12:55.480
It'd really be helpful if you just walk nice and slow.

00:12:55.480 --> 00:12:56.250
Yes, sir.

00:12:56.500 --> 00:13:00.210
Geez, where did he go?

00:13:02.790 --> 00:13:03.980
Huh?

00:13:05.330 --> 00:13:07.670
Tsuchiura-kun! Hihara-sempai!

00:13:07.670 --> 00:13:09.120
Oh, Hino, I'm glad you're here.

00:13:09.120 --> 00:13:10.160
Huh?

00:13:10.160 --> 00:13:16.740
Apparently some second-year Music Department kids saw Tsukimori-kun go outside.

00:13:16.740 --> 00:13:20.190
Outside? But it's almost his turn!

00:13:20.190 --> 00:13:23.480
Yeah. Which is why we're going to go look for him.

00:13:23.480 --> 00:13:25.240
I'll look too!

00:13:25.240 --> 00:13:27.770
Won't it be hard in those shoes?

00:13:27.770 --> 00:13:29.730
Yeah...

00:13:29.730 --> 00:13:32.590
I'll look around here again, then.

00:13:32.590 --> 00:13:33.310
Please.

00:13:33.310 --> 00:13:34.220
Yeah.

00:13:36.960 --> 00:13:40.330
Where'd you go off to, Tsukimori-kun?

00:13:45.580 --> 00:13:47.570
Shimizu...

00:13:53.280 --> 00:13:58.230
Walk slowly... Walk slowly...

00:13:58.230 --> 00:14:01.590
Shimizu, I'm really worried about you.

00:14:01.590 --> 00:14:03.750
Or maybe you're actually a stage veteran?

00:14:03.750 --> 00:14:06.770
Geez! Why did he go outside?

00:14:06.770 --> 00:14:09.800
And he left his violin just lying there!

00:14:11.220 --> 00:14:14.790
Would Tsukimori-kun leave his violin behind?

00:14:14.790 --> 00:14:17.470
Some second-year Music Department kids say they saw him.

00:14:18.230 --> 00:14:19.670
Music Department?

00:14:19.670 --> 00:14:22.660
That was the guy from before...

00:14:22.660 --> 00:14:25.830
Could it be that you're in love with him?

00:14:25.830 --> 00:14:27.840
What do you see in that guy?

00:14:27.840 --> 00:14:29.970
His personality is totally messed up.

00:14:30.690 --> 00:14:34.940
I'm overthinking things... They wouldn't have...

00:14:46.770 --> 00:14:48.390
Tsukimori-kun!

00:14:49.040 --> 00:14:55.330
Performer 6, from the Music Department, class 3-B, Azuma Yunoki-kun.

00:14:55.330 --> 00:14:59.190
Performing a Massenet composition, "Meditation from Thais."

00:15:19.890 --> 00:15:23.360
Tsukimori isn't back yet? He's up next!

00:15:26.010 --> 00:15:29.540
It won't open? And Yunoki-sempai is playing already!

00:15:29.950 --> 00:15:32.770
Who would do such a thing?

00:15:34.080 --> 00:15:39.490
I can't say who it is, but I can't say there aren't those who have a grudge against me.

00:15:46.430 --> 00:15:49.370
What do you mean that Tsukimori-kun isn't here?

00:15:49.370 --> 00:15:50.600
Well...

00:15:50.600 --> 00:15:52.330
Kanayan!

00:15:53.330 --> 00:15:54.300
Hihara!

00:15:54.300 --> 00:15:55.910
Did you find Tsukimori?

00:15:55.910 --> 00:15:57.610
No, not yet.

00:15:57.610 --> 00:16:01.100
Some guys said they saw him go outside, so Tsuchiura's out looking for him.

00:16:01.100 --> 00:16:03.930
Outside?! Are you serious?

00:16:03.930 --> 00:16:05.820
I'll go look again!

00:16:05.820 --> 00:16:06.850
H-Hey!

00:16:07.730 --> 00:16:08.820
Geez.

00:16:10.910 --> 00:16:13.580
It's too late.

00:16:13.580 --> 00:16:18.330
Moreover, I don't want those people to see me like this.

00:16:18.330 --> 00:16:20.750
As long as no one comes looking for me...

00:16:21.540 --> 00:16:24.720
Look for me? Who'd do a thing?

00:16:24.720 --> 00:16:28.330
They'd be losing a rival. Why would they look for me?

00:16:28.330 --> 00:16:29.850
It's idiotic.

00:16:30.460 --> 00:16:31.670
Tsukimori-kun!

00:16:33.630 --> 00:16:36.460
His violin is still lying there.

00:16:36.460 --> 00:16:39.170
Where did you go, Tsukimori-kun?

00:16:42.790 --> 00:16:43.980
He couldn't be...

00:16:44.670 --> 00:16:47.200
Why hasn't the next performer come out yet?

00:16:47.200 --> 00:16:49.210
Tsukimori-kun is the last performer, right?

00:16:49.210 --> 00:16:50.480
Isn't this taking too long?

00:16:57.520 --> 00:17:00.960
Damn it, where did he go?!

00:17:00.960 --> 00:17:02.500
How'd it work out?

00:17:03.200 --> 00:17:06.300
He's going to get disqualified for not showing up.

00:17:06.300 --> 00:17:09.500
Did we really have to lock him in there, though?

00:17:09.500 --> 00:17:12.240
Shut up! What's done is done.

00:17:12.240 --> 00:17:13.720
Yo.

00:17:14.560 --> 00:17:16.020
Thanks for before.

00:17:17.550 --> 00:17:19.540
We still can't find Tsukimori.

00:17:19.540 --> 00:17:25.530
Odd, isn't it? We've looked all over and can't find him.

00:17:25.530 --> 00:17:28.450
Perhaps he got scared and ran away?

00:17:28.450 --> 00:17:30.980
He's under a lot of pressure, I bet.

00:17:30.980 --> 00:17:33.530
Tsukimori run away?

00:17:33.780 --> 00:17:38.010
In any case, we've got nothing to do with it. Excuse us.

00:17:39.480 --> 00:17:43.350
Hey, you guys. You know something, don't you?

00:17:43.350 --> 00:17:48.870
Someone with as much pride as him would never run away.

00:17:48.870 --> 00:17:53.910
They still haven't found him? His parents came all the way here, too.

00:17:53.910 --> 00:17:55.480
Yeah...

00:17:55.480 --> 00:18:01.090
Excuse me, we can't keep everyone waiting much longer.

00:18:01.090 --> 00:18:07.050
Even if it's a competition, he has to respect the audience's time, no matter the reason.

00:18:07.450 --> 00:18:11.520
If he can't do that, he doesn't deserve to participate.

00:18:11.520 --> 00:18:12.400
But...

00:18:12.400 --> 00:18:16.980
As the participant, I am sure he understands this.

00:18:19.440 --> 00:18:22.500
Hey! Why is the door locked?!

00:18:24.420 --> 00:18:27.440
I'll go tell Kanazawa-sensei and get the key!

00:18:27.440 --> 00:18:29.640
Hino-san, it's OK.

00:18:29.640 --> 00:18:31.230
Tsukimori-kun?

00:18:31.230 --> 00:18:35.930
It's too late anyway. Didn't you want to drop a rival anyway?

00:18:36.920 --> 00:18:40.890
Wait a second! Is that how you see us?!

00:18:40.890 --> 00:18:42.070
It's a good thing for you.

00:18:42.070 --> 00:18:43.810
No, it isn't!

00:18:43.810 --> 00:18:47.260
There's no point in me going back and playing now.

00:18:47.740 --> 00:18:51.910
No point? I was looking forward to your performance.

00:18:51.910 --> 00:18:57.860
You play so well. I get so envious of your ability to play like that.

00:18:59.450 --> 00:19:04.220
And yet, you say there's no point in performing?

00:19:04.220 --> 00:19:06.280
Don't say that to me!

00:19:11.930 --> 00:19:16.300
I'll push the door, so please pull on it.

00:19:16.300 --> 00:19:17.520
OK!

00:19:21.130 --> 00:19:22.280
Kanayan!

00:19:22.280 --> 00:19:23.300
Tsuchiura.

00:19:23.300 --> 00:19:26.980
Why are you sending the audience home? There's a good reason...

00:19:27.450 --> 00:19:29.300
What's the meaning of this?

00:19:32.550 --> 00:19:36.760
Tsukimori! What the hell have you been doing all this time?!

00:19:37.720 --> 00:19:40.000
Tsukimori-kun hasn't performed yet,

00:19:40.000 --> 00:19:44.660
so why... why is everyone leaving the auditorium?!

00:19:45.410 --> 00:19:47.250
Hino, it's all right.

00:19:53.680 --> 00:19:55.870
I'm sorry to trouble you all.

00:19:59.930 --> 00:20:03.310
I get it... I get it, but...

00:20:03.310 --> 00:20:04.960
Just give it up, Hino.

00:20:05.430 --> 00:20:08.560
This doesn't sit right with me.

00:20:09.220 --> 00:20:11.940
It's not your fault. Don't worry about it.

00:20:11.940 --> 00:20:13.320
But!

00:20:13.320 --> 00:20:14.470
Ow!

00:20:14.980 --> 00:20:19.800
The competition isn't over yet. There's still lots of time left.

00:20:19.800 --> 00:20:22.960
You must be tired, too. Go home.

00:22:04.510 --> 00:22:06.300
The point of all this?

00:22:09.860 --> 00:22:10.770
Oh.

00:22:10.770 --> 00:22:13.060
You're Tsukimori-kun's mother!

00:22:13.060 --> 00:22:14.190
Hino-san.

00:22:14.190 --> 00:22:16.230
Thanks for coming today.

00:22:16.230 --> 00:22:19.730
No, thank you. You played us some lovely music.

00:22:19.730 --> 00:22:23.070
Your performance was free and wonderful.

00:22:23.900 --> 00:22:25.320
Thank you so much.

00:22:25.320 --> 00:22:30.380
Both you and Tsuchiura-kun are absolutely amazing for General Studies students.

00:22:31.640 --> 00:22:32.880
Goodbye.

00:22:32.880 --> 00:22:36.220
Umm, are you looking for Tsukimori-kun?

00:22:36.220 --> 00:22:39.000
Yes. Where could he have gone?

00:22:56.220 --> 00:23:00.550
He sounds different from how he usually does.

00:23:02.400 --> 00:23:05.650
When did he get so...

00:23:06.500 --> 00:23:10.450
It's Vitali's "Chaconne," isn't it? It sounds good.

00:23:10.870 --> 00:23:15.900
He's always been too absorbed into competitions and the like.

00:23:15.900 --> 00:23:19.350
I wish he could always play as free as he is now.

00:23:19.350 --> 00:23:21.120
What an awkward boy.

00:23:21.920 --> 00:23:26.340
My world is completely different from Tsukimori-kun's.

00:23:26.740 --> 00:23:31.690
He's in a world so distant and far away from mine.

00:23:36.240 --> 00:23:39.730
Lili's One Point Classic!

00:23:36.540 --> 00:23:39.710
Lili's One Point Classic

00:23:39.730 --> 00:23:44.520
"Virtuoso" means "master" or "expert" in Italian.

00:23:39.750 --> 00:23:46.670
Virtuoso

00:23:42.420 --> 00:23:46.670
Master

00:23:43.420 --> 00:23:46.670
Expert

00:23:44.520 --> 00:23:47.790
It usually refers to a musician with extraordinary technique.

00:23:47.790 --> 00:23:52.240
Paganini, a violinist in the early 19th century,

00:23:52.240 --> 00:23:55.360
who overwhelmed his audiences with his exceptional acrobatic technique,

00:23:55.360 --> 00:23:57.770
was, without a doubt, a virtuoso.

00:23:58.290 --> 00:24:00.200
OK, now time for a quiz.

00:24:00.200 --> 00:24:05.040
What word, meaning "master" in Italian, is used often to describe the conductor of an orchestra?

00:24:05.040 --> 00:24:09.920
Next Episode

00:24:05.630 --> 00:24:09.320
Everyone! Next episode, something incredibly shocking will take place!

00:24:09.320 --> 00:24:11.620
All the pork cutlet sandwiches at the stand will be sold out!

00:24:11.620 --> 00:24:14.430
That would be a matter of grave importance, wouldn't it?

